OneCamp patch for virtua 0.41.5, two changes. Each build here is one minified line, so each hunk replaces that
line. Drop the first when virtua moves to 0.53.5 or later; keep the second unless upstream drops the guard.

1. A touch the system cancels (touchcancel) ends the finger as touchend does. Backported from upstream virtua 0.53.5,
commit inokawa/virtua@11b11aceffe466d75e6f431f5f5a26be97be6cd0, "Handle touchcancel event" (#1026, 12 Oct 2026),
which adds the same listener beside touchend in src/core/driver.ts. Without it, after a cancelled touch the scroller
kept its rows' pointer events off until a touch ended normally, so a list on a phone missed a tap. The change adds
addEventListener("touchcancel", <the touchend handler>, {passive: true}) and its removeEventListener, with a comment.

2. The rows keep their pointer events while the list scrolls. virtua set pointer-events: none on its items from the
first scroll event until 150 ms after the last, so a press on a row that had just come to rest landed on the list and
did nothing: 14 of 14 presses 32-165 ms after a wheel scroll stopped (measured 27 Oct 2026). The change makes
both item containers' pointerEvents undefined, with a comment. app/virtuaPatch.test.ts fails when either change is
missing from node_modules.

